      "message": "I have just realized my previous implementation using `flat_hash_map` to store `BufferMapEntry` by value had a bug. If the hash map rehashed, it would invalidate all the linked list\u0027s pointers.\n\nThus, I have changed the hash map to store `unique_ptr` in the latest patchset. Its downside is that it would need an additional heap allocation for every buffer\u0027s remap. To reduce that I also added another list to recycle the allocated entries here. PTAL.\n\nAlternatively, we could store the MapEntry inside the Buffer class itself. WDYT?",
